course: dictionary
lesson: 13649
title: Inferior: not as good, or lower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inferior means not as good as something else, or of poor quality. Read «The shop sold inferior goods, and the toys broke on the first day.» The clue is broke on the first day. Things that break quickly are badly made, so inferior means poor quality. Check by swapping in "poor quality" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Inferior can also mean lower in rank or position. «The junior clerk was inferior to the manager, so he had to ask her before he made any decisions.» The clue is had to ask her. Someone who must ask permission is lower in rank.
explain: Be careful with people. Inferior describes things and positions, and it is never fair to say a person is worth less because of who they are. Stories about unfair treatment show how wrong this is, so we learn from them.
explain: Inferior is also a science word. «The inferior vena cava carries blood from the lower body back to the heart.» The clue is lower body. In body names, inferior means lower down.
fact: Inferior means not as good as something else, or of poor quality.
fact: Inferior means lower in rank or position, so an inferior is a person of lower rank, such as a junior worker.
fact: «Inferior goods» are cheap or badly made things.
fact: «Feel inferior» means to feel less good than other people, and «of inferior quality» means badly made.
fact: In science, inferior means lower down in the body, as in «the inferior vena cava».
exercise: «The shop sold inferior goods, and the toys broke on the first day.» What does inferior mean here? | *Poor quality, made badly | Very expensive and shiny | Lower down in the body | Brand new and bright
exercise: «The junior clerk was inferior to the manager.» What does inferior mean in this sentence? | Bright and shiny | *Lower in rank or position | Better at singing | Higher in rank
exercise: A science book says «the inferior vena cava». What does inferior mean in that name? | Made of glass | *Lower down in the body | Loud noise | Very kind
test: «Ella said her old bike was inferior to Sam's new one, because it was slower and kept breaking.» What does inferior mean? | Better than | *Not as good as | Painted red | Faster than
test: Jayden says, «Nobody should be treated as inferior just because of who they are.» What does this teach us? | Rank decides who is kind | *Unfair treatment of people for who they are is wrong | Some people are worth less, so treating them unfairly is fine | Inferior means happy
exam: «The inferior cloth tore when Mia pulled it, so she bought a stronger one.» Which word tells you the cloth was of poor quality? | *Inferior | Bought | Pulled | Stronger
